7,127,51.9,1,0,26,2,103.6,83,11,84,7.6,0,32]},{"id":"401856749","date":"2026-11-21","week":12,"type":"reg","home":true,"opp":"WOF","oppName":"Wofford Terriers","result":"W","score":"59-17","values":[19,20,367,95,5,0,55,1,331.6,96.8,1,6,6,0,6]}]}},"summaryLabel":"2026 season stats","news":[{"headline":"Georgia flips script on Trinidad Chambliss, dominates Ole Miss in statement win","description":"No. 2 Georgia finally contained Ole Miss QB Trinidad Chambliss, holding him without a passing touchdown en route to a 42-7 blowout win over the No. 10 Rebels.","published":"2026-11-08T16:10:11.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50417639/georgia-flips-script-trinidad-chambliss-dominates-ole-miss-statement-win","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Mark Schlabach","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Breaking down the Heisman race: How Week 10 could change everything","description":"Pamela Maldonado breaks down where things stand on the Heisman odds board with a new favorite taking over.","published":"2026-11-04T02:23:18.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/50360375/college-football-heisman-2026-odds-favorites-picks-week-10","type":"Story","byline":"Pamela Maldonado","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"USC band won't perform at UCLA football game after members vandalized campus","description":"The USC Trojan Marching Band will not perform during Saturday's rivalry game vs. UCLA after members of the band vandalized a portion of UCLA's campus.","published":"2026-11-26T04:02:46.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50600615/usc-band-perform-members-vandalized-ucla-campus","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Paolo Uggetti","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Kent State TD overturned by replay was incorrect decision, MAC says","description":"A Kent State touchdown catch should not have been overturned by replay to incomplete at the end of Tuesday's 17-12 loss to Eastern Michigan, the Mid-American Conference said Wednesday.","published":"2026-11-25T23:05:40.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50597875/kent-state-td-overturned-replay-was-incorrect-mac-says","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 College Football Playoff National Championship odds","description":"Odds and futures to win the 2027 College Football Playoff National Championship.","published":"2026-11-25T19:44:57.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/47664633/2027-college-football-playoff-national-championship-odds-futures","type":"Story","byline":"Doug Greenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Chris Creighton out as coach at Eastern Michigan after 13 seasons","description":"Chris Creighton is out as head coach at Eastern Michigan after 13 seasons with the school.","published":"2026-11-25T19:05:05.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50595706/creighton-coach-eastern-michigan-13-seasons","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Judge denies SEC's request for TRO against LSU in Dec. 3 vote","description":"A federal judge denied the SEC's request for a temporary restraining order to keep LSU from interfering with a Dec. 3 vote of presidents and chancellors on whether to remove the school from the conference.","published":"2026-11-25T20:02:54.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-sports/story/_/id/50595702/judge-denies-sec-request-tro-lsu-dec-3-vote","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Week 13 Game Day Kickoff: Nothing compares to the outright hatred of a rival","description":"What to expect in Rivalry Week, from top games and players to teams on upset alert.","published":"2026-11-25T19:44:59.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/page/gamedaykickoff112526/week-13-top-games-upsets-preview","type":"Story","byline":"David Hale","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Oklahoma State extends Morris with new 6-year deal","description":"Oklahoma State and head coach Eric Morris have agreed to a new six-year deal that will extend his contract through the 2032 season, sources told ESPN's Pete Thamel on Wednesday.","published":"2026-11-25T17:00:56.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50594432/sources-oklahoma-state-extends-morris-new-six-year-deal","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Where is 'College GameDay'? 2026 schedule, locations, recaps","description":"What is the \"College GameDay\" schedule? Find out more about where the program will be each week of the 2026 college football season.","published":"2026-11-25T15:16:09.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/49783645/where-college-gameday-2026-schedule-locations-recaps","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4911529/trinidad-chambliss","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trinidad_Chambliss"},"pick":{"pick":20,"round":1,"team":"CLE","provisional":true},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Trinidad Chambliss","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trinidad_Chambliss","description":"American football player (born 2002)","touched":"2026-11-22T23:50:21Z","intro":"Trinidad Jay Chambliss (; born August 24, 2002) is an American college football quarterback for the Ole Miss Rebels. He previously played for the Ferris State Bulldogs, leading the 2024 Bulldogs to the Division II national championship.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Chambliss attended Forest Hills Northern High School in Grand Rapids, Michigan. As a senior, he threw for 1,610 yards and 17 touchdowns. After graduating high school, he committed to play college football at Ferris State University."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"FERRIS STATE\nAs a junior in 2024, Chambliss threw for 2,925 yards and 26 touchdowns and rushed for 1,019 yards and 25 touchdowns, leading Ferris State to a Division II national championship. In the national championship game against Valdosta State, he combined for five touchdowns in the 49–14 victory. As a result of his play, Chambliss was named the Great Lakes Intercollegiate Athletic Conference Player of the Year and a finalist for the Harlon Hill Trophy. Following the conclusion of the season, he entered the transfer portal.\n\nOLE MISS\nIn April 2025, Chambliss announced his decision to transfer to the University of Mississippi to play for the Ole Miss Rebels. He entered the season as the backup to Austin Simmons. In the season opener against Georgia State, he completed four passes for 59 yards and a touchdown. Following an injury to Simmons, Chambliss was named the Rebels' starting quarterback against Arkansas. In his first start for Ole Miss, he combined for 415 total yards and three touchdowns in a 41–35 triumph over Arkansas. In the Egg Bowl against Mississippi State, Chambliss completed 23 passes for 359 yards and four touchdowns, leading the Rebels to a 38–19 victory and clinching a spot in the College Football Playoff. At the conclusion of the regular season, he was named the SEC Newcomer of the Year and recipient of the Conerly Trophy. In the first round of the playoffs against Tulane, Chambliss threw for 282 yards and combined for three total touchdowns in a win. In the 2026 Sugar Bowl, he completed 30 passes for a season-high 362 yards and two touchdowns, leading Ole Miss to a 39–34 upset victory in a rematch against Georgia; he was named the game's offensive MVP for his efforts.\nIn November 2025, Ole Miss filed a waiver request with the NCAA to allow Chambliss a sixth year of eligibility, as he did not play during his sophomore season at Ferris State in 2022 due to persistent respiratory issues. On January 9, 2026, the NCAA denied the request, ending his college eligibility. Ole Miss filed an appeal with the NCAA. On January 16, lawyers representing Chambliss sued the NCAA in Mississippi state court, seeking preliminary and permanent injunctions that would allow him to play an additional season. On February 5, 2026, Chambliss' appeal was rejected again. Following another appeal, a judge granted Chambliss an injunction on February 12, 2026, allowing him a sixth year of college eligibility.\nChambliss returned to Ole Miss in 2026 rather than enter the 2026 NFL draft. In the season opener, the Music City Kickoff against No. 24 Louisville, he threw for 336 yards, three touchdowns, and an interception while rushing for 60 yards and a touchdown. Against his former head coach Lane Kiffin and No. 7 LSU, Chambliss led the Rebels to a 32–24 victory, completing 33 passes for 363 yards and accounting for three touchdowns."}]}}